      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. so it was kind of like a perfect storm of things working together. but i've also heard some people argue that the heavy union influence actually ended up hurting the economy in the long run by making things too expensive or making companies less competitive. do you think those critics have a point, or are they just trying to downplay the progress that was made?",
